{title: He Leadeth Me}
{artist: Joseph Gilmore & William Bradbury}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
He [D]leadeth me! O [G]blessed [D]thought, O words with heavenly [A]comfort fraught;
what[D]e'er I do, wher[G]e'er I [D]be, still 'tis God's [A]hand that [D]leadeth me.

Chorus
He [D]leadeth me, he [A]leadeth me, by [D]his own hand he [A]leadeth me;
his [D]faithful follower [G]I would [D]be, for by his [A]hand he [D]leadeth me.

Verse 2
Sometimes mid [D]scenes of deepest gloom, Sometimes where [G]Eden's bowers [D]bloom, By waters still, ov'r troubled sea, Still 'tis His [A]hand that leadeth me.
He leadeth me, He leadeth me, By His own hand [D]He leadeth me; His faithful follow'r I would [A]be, For by His [D]hand He leadeth me.

Verse 3
Lord, I [D]would place my hand in Thine, [G]Nor ever [D]murmur nor repine; Content, whatever lot I see, Since 'tis [A]my God that leadeth
me. He leadeth me, He leadeth me, By His own [D]hand He leadeth me; His faithful follow'r I would [A]be, For by His [D]hand He leadeth me.

Verse 4
And when [D]my task on earth is done, When [G]by Thy [D]grace the vict'ry's won, E'en death's cold wave I will not [A]flee, Since God through
Jordan leadeth me. He leadeth me, He leadeth me, By His [D]own hand He leadeth me; His faithful follow'r I [A]would be, For by His [D]hand He leadeth me.
